  "prompt": "I have 4 completely independent work streams to run in parallel. NOTHING is given to you directly — every value and identifier lives in the system's records and must be resolved by following references from one record to the next. For each item, start from the named worklist and dereference step by step until you reach the concrete value, then act. (A) SHARE FILES: From sharing worklist `sharing_worklist_wl2`, share each file that is NOT already shared (skip already_shared on its dereferenced record — the worklist also lists already-shared / archived look-alikes). For each real one, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then its file record for the file id and permission, then its recipient person to an account for the email, and share it. Then, from worklist `append_to_file_wl1`, append the reconciliation note to the file: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `reply_to_email_wl1`, reply to the vendor onboarding email: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (B) PURGE EMAILS: From cleanup worklist `cleanup_worklist_wl2`, delete each flagged email that is NOT pinned (skip pinned on its dereferenced record — the list mixes pinned look-alikes). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then delete it. Then, from worklist `cancel_calendar_event_wl1`, cancel the stale budget review event: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `remove_calendar_event_participants_wl1`, remove the departed contractor from the sprint planning event: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (C) RELOCATE EVENTS: From relocation worklist `relocation_worklist_wl2`, relocate each CONFIRMED event (skip confirmed=false — the list also lists unconfirmed look-alikes). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and its organizer, then set the location. Then, from worklist `add_calendar_event_participants_wl1`, add the new hire to the design sync event: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `reschedule_calendar_event_wl1`, reschedule the client demo event: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). (D) NOTIFY STAFF: From notify worklist `notify_worklist_wl2`, email a status note to each staff member NOT already notified (skip notified on its dereferenced record — the list mixes already-notified look-alikes). For each, resolve every value it requires by following the record references, then send it. Then, from worklist `create_file_wl1`, create the onboarding checklist file: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). Then, from worklist `unshare_file_wl1`, revoke the departed collaborator's access to the shared file: pick the real item (SKIP the superseded look-alike), then resolve every value it requires by following the record references, and act with those resolved values (never the worklist ref itself). None of these 4 streams depend on each other, so run them concurrently. For EVERY item: resolve each target FRESH by chaining through the records at the moment you act — never guess, and never reuse a value you read earlier.",
